            "type": "image",
            "bbox": [
                0.544,
                0.627,
                0.92,
                0.676
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": null
        },
        {
            "type": "image_footnote",
            "bbox": [
                0.585,
                0.679,
                0.823,
                0.686
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Experienced Occasional"
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph_title",
            "bbox": [
                0.036,
                0.718,
                0.641,
                0.735
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "TO MASTER M&A IN A DOWNTURN, BUYERS SHOULD FOLLOW A SET OF IMPERATIVES"
        },
        {
            "type": "image",
            "bbox": [
                0.355,
                0.743,
                0.553,
                0.789
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": null
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph_title",
            "bbox": [
                0.359,
                0.792,
                0.49,
                0.799
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Be prepared"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.358,
                0.8,
                0.629,
                0.825
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Put in place an ongoing target-screening process that covers strategic priorities — it’s a no-regrets move",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "image",
            "bbox": [
                0.175,
                0.833,
                0.369,
                0.866
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": null
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph_title",
            "bbox": [
                0.166,
                0.865,
                0.249,
                0.872
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Be bold"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.164,
                0.872,
                0.461,
                0.897
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Boldly pursue downturn M&A opportunities if they materialize — downturns are, on average, good times to make deals",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "image",
            "bbox": [
                0.66,
                0.853,
                0.833,
                0.877
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": null
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph_title",
            "bbox": [
                0.633,
                0.881,
                0.819,
                0.888
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Be transformative"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.631,
                0.889,
                0.915,
                0.913
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Use transformational deals to stay ahead of the curve and accelerate out of the recession when the upturn starts",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "footer",
            "bbox": [
                0.027,
                0.943,
                0.971,
                0.96
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Source: This infographic is based on BCG's 2019 M&A Report: Downturns Are a Better Time for Deal Hunting, September 2019 (https://www.bcg.com/publications/2019/mergers-and-acquisitions-report-shows-downturns-a-better-time-for-deal-hunting.aspx). The data set used for the analyses in BCG's M&A research comprises approximately 759,000 deals, covering the period 1980 through 2018. We collected and collated data from a variety of financial databases, including Refinitiv (formerly Thomson Reuters Financial & Risk), Datastream, Worldscope, and S&P Capital IQ, as well as our own proprietary data and analytics. For the analyses in the report, we focused on roughly $1,600 deals that met our study criteria and involved transfers of majority shares, including spinoffs, with a transaction value of at least $250 million. The data set covers all acquisitions—of both private and public targets—by public buyers."
        },
